    "number": 3172,
    "title": "Race condition in executor when canceling before spin",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/issues/3172",
    "body": "### Generated by Generative AI\n\nNo\n\n### Operating System:\n\nresolute, in the buildfarm\n\n### ROS version or commit hash:\n\nrolling\n\n### RMW implementation (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### RMW Configuration (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### Client library (if applicable):\n\nrclcpp\n\n### 'ros2 doctor --report' output\n\n<details><summary>ros2 doctor --report</summary>\n\n```console\n<COPY OUTPUT HERE>\n```\n</details>\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce issue\n\nfirst surfaced in https://github.com/ros-perception/image_common/pull/421 \n\n### Expected behavior\n\nthe executor does not hang indefinitely if cancelled before it spins\n\n### Actual behavior\n\ncopied from the issue:\n\nTearDown() calls executor->cancel() , setting the executor's internal spinning atomic flag to false .\nThe background thread subsequently starts executing spin() , which performs spinning.exchange(true) . This unconditionally sets spinning back to true .\nThe executor enters the spin loop and blocks on wait_for_work() indefinitely, as cancel() has already been called. The thread never joins, causing the test suite to hang.\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Generated by Generative AI</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">No</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Operating System:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">resolute, in the buildfarm</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">ROS version or commit hash:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">rolling</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW implementation (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW Configuration (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Client library (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">rclcpp</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">'ros2 doctor --report' output</h3>\n<details><summary>ros2 doctor --report</summary>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-shell-session notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&lt;COPY OUTPUT HERE&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">&lt;COPY OUTPUT HERE&gt;</span></pre></div>\n</details>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Steps to reproduce issue</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">first surfaced in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4554896568\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/ros-perception/image_common/issues/421\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/ros-perception/image_common/pull/421/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/ros-perception/image_common/pull/421\">ros-perception/image_common#421</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Expected behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">the executor does not hang indefinitely if cancelled before it spins</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Actual behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">copied from the issue:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">TearDown() calls executor-&gt;cancel() , setting the executor's internal spinning atomic flag to false .<br>\nThe background thread subsequently starts executing spin() , which performs spinning.exchange(true) . This unconditionally sets spinning back to true .<br>\nThe executor enters the spin loop and blocks on wait_for_work() indefinitely, as cancel() has already been called. The thread never joins, causing the test suite to hang.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional information</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>",
