      "body": "Yeah, its makes sense to fix this.\nI remember adding a \"wait until spinning\" before calling cancel in some tests in rclcpp.\n\nWhat's the expected behavior though?\nHow to distinguish between the race condition and a legit use-case where an executor is cancelled and then \"re-spinned\" some time later?\n\nWe could  handle that with new APIs but I don't really like it\n\n\n",
      "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yeah, its makes sense to fix this.<br>\nI remember adding a \"wait until spinning\" before calling cancel in some tests in rclcpp.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What's the expected behavior though?<br>\nHow to distinguish between the race condition and a legit use-case where an executor is cancelled and then \"re-spinned\" some time later?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We could  handle that with new APIs but I don't really like it</p>",
